    "text": "© 2026 SaturdayDownSouth.com Home > News > Sports > How to Watch Missouri vs Miami (FL): TV Channel and Schedule Info for the Tigers & Hurricanes Postseason Matchup Ad Disclosure This article/post contains references to products or services from one or more of our advertisers or partners. We may receive compensation when you click on links to those products or services. The postseason features a first-round West Region matchup between the 10-seed Missouri Tigers and the 7-seed Miami Hurricanes. Head coach Dennis Gates leads Missouri into this contest against head coach Jai Lucas and a Miami squad that enters the game ranked 25th in the AP Top 25. Miami holds a 25-8 record after going 13-5 in the Atlantic Coast Conference. Missouri brings a 20-12 overall record and a 10-8 mark from the Southeastern Conference. Watch Missouri vs. Miami (FL) on Sling TV. While officially a neutral site game, the Tigers hold a distinct geographic advantage. The teams meet in St. Louis, Missouri, which sits roughly 100 miles from the Missouri campus. This creates an interesting dynamic as the SEC and ACC programs compete to advance. For fans preparing for the game, we have all the essential details covered. Continue reading to find the scheduled tip-off time, the exact location information, and how to watch the live television broadcast and stream the game as the Tigers and Hurricanes take the court. Game Preview and Market Outlook As the Tigers and Hurricanes prepare to face off, prediction markets are closely watching the implied probability of a Miami victory. Miami holds the higher seed, but Missouri has the regional advantage of playing close to home. Fans looking to turn their basketball knowledge into a prediction market opportunity can head over to Kalshi to find value in the outcome of this matchup. Whether you are backing the Hurricanes or the Tigers, you can check the odds and take a position on the outright winner using a Kalshi promo code. When is Missouri vs Miami (FL)? What time does it start? The postseason matchup between the Missouri Tigers and Miami (FL) Hurricanes is scheduled for March 20, 2026. Tip-off is set for 10:10 PM ET. The game takes place at the Enterprise Center in St. Louis, Missouri. Fans watching from home can catch the live television broadcast to see who advances to the next round. Where is the Missouri vs Miami (FL) game? This first-round matchup is being played at the Enterprise Center, located in St. Louis, Missouri. While this is officially a neutral site contest for the NCAA Tournament, the proximity to the Missouri campus makes it a very favorable location for the Tigers. The Miami (FL) Hurricanes are designated as the home team, and the Missouri Tigers serve as the away team for this game. How can I Watch Missouri vs Miami (FL)? Fans looking to follow the postseason matchup between the Missouri Tigers and the Miami (FL) Hurricanes can watch the game on live television. This neutral site contest is scheduled to be broadcast nationally on the truTV network. Viewers can tune in directly to truTV for full live coverage as the game gets underway at 10:10 PM ET. How can I Stream Missouri vs Miami (FL)? The television broadcast for this postseason matchup is on truTV. Viewers can stream the game directly through the truTV app or the network website by logging in with a valid cable or satellite provider credential. Live sports broadcasts on truTV are also accessible through the HBO Max streaming platform. If you do not have a traditional pay television subscription, you can stream the game using various live television streaming services. Platforms such as Sling TV, YouTube TV, Hulu + Live TV, and DirecTV Stream include truTV in their channel packages. This allows fans to easily watch the Missouri Tigers and Miami (FL) Hurricanes online. Who will Win Missouri vs Miami (FL)? Data from Kalshi on March 18th. Based on the current prediction market odds, the Miami (FL) Hurricanes are the statistical favorites to win this postseason matchup. Miami has an implied win probability of 53.0%. The Missouri Tigers enter the contest with odds that represent a 47.0% chance of securing the victory. These probabilities indicate that the Hurricanes are slightly more likely to win outright, though the margins reflect a closely projected game between the two programs. Creative Manager and Writer at Sportradar. Craig has previously worked as a camera operator and video director in radio and television, as well as a content coordinator in the non-profit sector. You might also like...",
